{#-
  Who sends every email, in law. The one place these details are written
  for email: change them here and every footer follows.

  Both brands are trading names of the same company, so nothing here
  depends on the brand but the name it trades under, which comes from the
  theme. Import with context, so `t` is in scope:

    {% import "_company.html.j2" as company with context %}

  The public site states the same details on its company information
  page (frontend/public_pages/src/pages/company-information.tsx), and
  the terms and the privacy policy state them under docs/docs/legal/.
  Those are separate documents and are changed by hand.
-#}
{% set legal_name = "Bailey Medics Ltd" %}
{% set company_number = "15604352" %}
{% set registered_office = "Brooklands Place, Unit 5, Brooklands Road, Sale, Cheshire, M33 3SD" %}

{#-
  The sentence a footer ends with. Short for an email somebody asked
  for. With `registered=true` it adds the company number and registered
  office, which a newsletter carries because marketing email must say
  who sent it and where they can be written to.
-#}
{% macro trading_line(registered=false) -%}
{{ t.sender_name }} is a trading name of {{ legal_name }}.{% if registered %} Company number {{ company_number }}. {{ registered_office }}.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
